    html: |
      <section class="page-hero" style="background-image:url('assets/img/dest-zhangjiajie.png');"><div class="container"><span class="breadcrumb"><a href="index.html">Home</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <a href="tours.html">Destinations</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Zhangjiajie</span><h1>Zhangjiajie <span class="zh" style="font-family:var(--font-zh);font-size:0.65em;color:var(--gold);">张家界</span></h1><p>Zhangjiajie is where gravity seems optional. Thousands of quartz-sandstone pillars punch through the clouds — the real-life landscape that inspired Avatar's floating mountains.</p></div></section>
  - label: "Why visit Zhangjiajie?"
    html: |
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div class="split-media reveal"><img src="assets/img/dest-zhangjiajie.png" alt="Zhangjiajie" /><div class="seal-stamp" aria-hidden="true">张<br/>家</div></div><div class="split-copy reveal reveal-d1"><span class="eyebrow">Epic Nature</span><h2 class="display-h2">Why visit Zhangjiajie?</h2><p>Zhangjiajie is where gravity seems optional. Thousands of sandstone pillars punch through the clouds — the real-life landscape that inspired Avatar's floating mountains. Cross a glass bridge 300 metres above a canyon, then descend into the lantern-lit alleys of Fenghuang old town.</p><p>Nowhere in China feels more like another planet. Pair the peaks with the Tuojiang River's glowing water town and you get a journey that is at once thunderous and tender.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Zhangjiajie at a glance"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;"><div class="container"><div class="stat-strip"><div class="stat-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);"><div class="reveal"><div class="stat-num">3,000+</div><div class="stat-label">Quartz-sandstone pillars rising from the mist</div></div><div class="reveal reveal-d1"><div class="stat-num">1,080 m</div><div class="stat-label">Height of Avatar Hallelujah Mountain (Yuanjiajie)</div></div><div class="reveal reveal-d2"><div class="stat-num">300 m</div><div class="stat-label">Height of the glass bridge above the Grand Canyon</div></div><div class="reveal reveal-d3"><div class="stat-num">1,300</div><div class="stat-label">Years of Fenghuang ancient town's riverside history</div></div></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Iconic experiences in Zhangjiajie"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="background:var(--white);"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow centered">Must-See Sights</span><h2 class="display-h2">Iconic experiences in Zhangjiajie</h2></div><div class="feature-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);"><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Avatar Hallelujah Mountain</h3><p>The 1,080 m pillar that inspired the movie. Ride the Bailong Elevator — the world's tallest outdoor lift — up its face.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Tianzi Mountain</h3><p>The 'Emperor's Mountain' offers the most dramatic panorama — especially at sunrise over a sea of clouds.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Glass Bridge</h3><p>Walk on transparent glass 300 m above the Zhangjiajie Grand Canyon. Unforgettable — and not for the faint-hearted.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Tianmen Mountain</h3><p>A cable car to a natural sky-hole, a cliff-hugging glass walkway, and the vertiginous 999-step staircase.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Golden Whip Stream</h3><p>A flat forest trail along a clear stream, flanked by pillars — the most peaceful walk in the park.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Fenghuang Ancient Town</h3><p>A 1,300-year-old riverside town of stilted wooden houses and stone bridges — pure lantern-lit romance.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "The Tujia Table"
    html: |
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div class="split-copy reveal"><span class="eyebrow">Food Capital</span><h2 class="display-h2">The Tujia Table</h2><p>The food of western Hunan is rustic and smoky. The Tujia and Miao minorities cure their pork over woodsmoke (la rou) and simmer sour fish soups that wake the palate. Our guides take you to village kitchens where the wok has been fired for generations.</p><p>Hearty, honest and a little fiery — it's the perfect fuel after a day among the peaks.</p><ul class="tour-highlights" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:10px;"><li><strong>La rou (cured pork)</strong> — wood-smoked belly, the region's signature</li><li><strong>Sour fish soup (suantang yu)</strong> — tangy, warming, uniquely western Hunan</li><li><strong>Glutinous rice cakes</strong> — pounded and grilled, a festival staple</li><li><strong>Wild mountain vegetables</strong> — foraged greens lightly stir-fried</li><li><strong>Fenghuang ginger candy</strong> — a sweet-spicy souvenir</li></ul></div><div class="split-media reveal reveal-d1"><img src="assets/img/zhangjiajie-food.png" alt="Tujia minority feast" /><div class="seal-stamp" aria-hidden="true">山<br/>味</div></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "A perfect 4-day journey"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="background:var(--paper-deep);"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow centered">Sample Itinerary</span><h2 class="display-h2">A perfect 4-day journey</h2><p>Every journey we design is tailor-made — this is a favourite starting point.</p></div><div class="steps-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:22px;"><div class="step reveal"><span class="step-num">01</span><h3>Arrival &amp; Sky Gate</h3><p>Private transfer, then Tianmen Mountain — cable car to the sky-hole, the glass walkway, and the 999-step staircase.</p></div><div class="step reveal reveal-d1"><span class="step-num">02</span><h3>Avatar Mountains</h3><p>Yuanjiajie (the Avatar pillars) by Bailong Elevator, then Tianzi Mountain for the classic sea-of-clouds panorama.</p></div><div class="step reveal reveal-d2"><span class="step-num">03</span><h3>Streams &amp; Glass</h3><p>A forest walk along Golden Whip Stream, then the Grand Canyon Glass Bridge — 300 m of transparent bravery.</p></div><div class="step reveal reveal-d3"><span class="step-num">04</span><h3>Fenghuang Farewell</h3><p>Scenic transfer to Fenghuang ancient town, a lantern-lit evening by the Tuojiang River, then your onward flight.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Zhangjiajie after dark"
    html: |
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div class="split-media reveal"><img src="assets/img/zhangjiajie-night.png" alt="Fenghuang ancient town at night" /></div><div class="split-copy reveal reveal-d1"><span class="eyebrow">Night Views</span><h2 class="display-h2">Zhangjiajie after dark</h2><p>As night falls the granite giants vanish into shadow and the real romance begins in Fenghuang. Stilted wooden houses along the Tuojiang River glow with lanterns, their reflections trembling on the water, while Tujia song drifts from the bridges.</p><ul class="tour-highlights" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:10px;"><li>Fenghuang lantern town — stilted houses glowing over the Tuojiang River</li><li>Tujia cultural evening — song, dance and drumming</li><li>Zhangjiajie night-market snacks and street BBQ</li><li>A riverside bar with a view of the lit old town</li></ul></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Beyond the city"
    html: |
      <section class="section" style="background:var(--white);"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="eyebrow centered">Nearby Escapes</span><h2 class="display-h2">Beyond the park</h2></div><div class="feature-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);"><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M3 18l6-8 4 5 3-4 5 7z"/><path d="M3 21h18"/></svg></div><h3>Furong Town</h3><p>A 'waterfall town' draped over cliffs, its tiered houses and silk cascade lit beautifully after dark. 2 h away.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg></div><h3>Dehang Miaozhai</h3><p>A Miao minority hamlet folded into a gorge — terraced fields, silver embroidery and warm home-cooked meals.</p></div><div class="card feature-card reveal"><div class="feature-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 18h16M6 18V8l6-4 6 4v10"/><path d="M10 18v-4h4v4"/></svg></div><h3>Mengdong River</h3><p>A drifting trip through jade gorges and bat caves — a playful counterpoint to the high drama of the pillars.</p></div></div></div></section>
  - label: "Good to know"
    html: |
      <section class="commit-band section"><div class="container"><div class="section-head reveal" style="margin-bottom:20px;"><span class="eyebrow centered">Travel Tips</span><h2 class="display-h2">Good to know before you go</h2></div><div class="commit-grid" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;"><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Fog is magic</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">Misty days give the best 'Avatar' photos. We build buffer days so the weather can't ruin your shot.</p></div></div><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Heights</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">The glass bridge and skywalk aren't for everyone — we always offer a comfortable alternative route.</p></div></div><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>On foot</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">The trails are real walks. Good grip shoes and moderate fitness make the peaks far more enjoyable.</p></div></div><div class="commit-item reveal"><span class="commit-check">✓</span><div><strong>Weather</strong><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);margin-top:6px;">A mountain microclimate — cool and wet even in summer. Pack layers and a rain shell; the cable cars do the climbs.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
